From: Tianyu9748 <54686548+Tianyu9748@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:02:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/26] [Diffusion] Per-prompt text-embedding cache

TextEncodingStage.encode_text gains an optional process-wide host LRU
(TextEmbeddingCache), off unless SGLANG_WL_EMBED_CACHE_BYTES (bytes) is
> 0. One entry per prompt; key = (text-encoder identity: model path(s),
revision, stage / pipeline-config / encoder / tokenizer / pre- and
postprocessing objects, encoder dtypes, tokenizer and encoder settings,
conditioning-weights epoch, autocast state; call settings: encoder
indices, masks, return type, output device and dtype, max_length and the
other overrides; sha256 of the prompt). An entry holds the prompt's
encoder output exactly as produced (pinned host copies); a hit copies it
back to the original device, dtype and strides, so hits are bitwise the
miss. Eviction is least-recently-used by bytes; hits, misses, stores,
evictions and bypasses are counted.

A prompt list (LongLive 2.0 block prompts, batch.prompt = block_prompts)
is served one distinct prompt at a time and the rows are stacked in list
order: equal to one encoder call per prompt (as LongLive 1.0 and the
causal-Wan profile stage encode), never dependent on the cache state, and
a request one shot deeper encodes only its new prompt. The umt5 encoder
is not batch-invariant, so these rows need not equal one batched call's;
single-prompt calls are unchanged. Calls the cache cannot serve (stack
return type, grad or compile, CUDA graph capture, more than one rank,
outputs that are not one row per prompt) take the plain call (bypass).

With the request's workload timer bound (TextEncodingStage.forward),
encoder calls and cache misses are timed as text_encode spans and hits
as text_encode_cached. New unit test test/unit/test_wl_embed_cache.py.
